ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES

The AI StudyBuddy application implements role-based access control to provide different privileges for Students and Administrators. JWT authentication is used to identify authenticated users, while role-based authorization controls access to specific system operations.

Student

Students are the primary users of the AI StudyBuddy application. They can register and securely log in to the system. After authentication, students can upload and manage their study materials and use AI-powered services to generate summaries, flashcards, quizzes, and personalized study plans. Students can view their previously generated resources and manage their learning content through the dashboard. Access to study resources is restricted to the authenticated user's data.

Administrator

Administrators are responsible for managing the overall application. They can view and manage registered users, monitor application usage, and perform system-level management operations. Administrative APIs are protected using JWT authentication and role-based authorization so that only users with the Administrator role can access them.

User Flow

The AI StudyBuddy application begins with user registration or login. During login, the server verifies the user's credentials and generates a JWT containing the user's identity and role. The token is used for subsequent protected API requests.

After successful authentication, the user is directed to the appropriate dashboard based on their role. Students can upload study materials and select AI-powered features such as summary generation, flashcard generation, quiz generation, and personalized study-plan generation.

The selected study content is retrieved from MongoDB and sent to the AI service layer. The AI service communicates with the Google Gemini API and receives the generated learning resource. The generated resource is returned to the backend, stored in MongoDB when required, and displayed on the student's dashboard.

Administrators are provided with a separate management interface through which they can manage users and perform system-level operations. This role-based flow ensures that users can access only the features and resources permitted by their assigned roles.

